nd transformers.\n- **Debt market:** It is open but more expensive. Utility bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 2026 to 165bp. Norvane priced a C$1.1B bond comfortably, so a stronger issuer can still borrow.\n- **Equity market:** It is weak. Two utility share offerings were cut back in size. Pellham withdrew its C$2.4B equity offering after demand fell short.\n- **Pellham's response:** It plans to cut 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and defer two substation programmes until financing improves. That suggests it could not close its funding gap with debt alone.\n- **Norvane:** It looks able to fund its smaller increase through bonds. I only have the one C$1.1B deal to go on, so I can't say whether that covers its whole plan.\n\nThe sources don't give total funding needs, leverage or credit ratings. I can't say how much debt capacity Pellham has left, or whether it could have issued bonds instead of cutting spending.\n\nBecause Pellham is the largest single buyer of grid equipment in Caldria, its cuts could reduce equipment demand across the country.\n\nThe three documents behind this are `utility-capex-2027`, `utility-credit` and `pellham-offering`.","ttft_ms":3411,"type":"result","duration_ms":14031,"uuid":"97ade2f7-c389-46ec-bfa4-655981f10c5d","ttft_stream_ms":2895,"time_to_request_ms":99,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":7,"system_prompt":15,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":6,"input_attachments":19,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":3,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":7,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":8,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":9,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":4,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":3,"request_build":6},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":48,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":80,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":201,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":12